### Goal Model Decomposition

#### Goals Table

| Goal ID | Goal Title | Text | Runtime Annotation | Goal Type | Relation | Justification |
|--------|------------|------|--------------------|-----------|----------|----------------|
| G1     | Deliver Required Resources | Ensure resources are collected from storage and delivered to the specified location. | ; | Achieve | - | The mission's primary objective is to successfully deliver resources, making it an achieve goal. |
| G2     | Collect Resources from Storage | Gather required resources from their respective storage locations. | - | Perform | G1 | This goal is a perform goal as it involves executing the collection actions. |
| G3     | Deliver Collected Resources | Transport collected resources to the specified delivery location. | - | Perform | G1 | This goal is a perform goal as it involves executing the delivery actions. |

#### Tasks Table

| Task ID | Task Title | Text | Relation | Location | Number of Robots | Justification |
|---------|------------|------|----------|----------|-------------------|----------------|
| AT1.1   | Collect from Storage A | Retrieve resources from Storage A. | AND | Storage A | 1 | Each storage location is handled by a single robot to ensure precise retrieval. |
| AT1.2   | Collect from Storage B | Retrieve resources from Storage B. | AND | Storage B | 1 | Each storage location is handled by a single robot to ensure precise retrieval. |
| AT2.1   | Deliver to Location A | Transport resources to Delivery Point A. | AND | Delivery Point A | 1 | Each delivery point is handled by a single robot to ensure accurate delivery. |
| AT2.2   | Deliver to Location B | Transport resources to Delivery Point B. | AND | Delivery Point B | 1 | Each delivery point is handled by a single robot to ensure accurate delivery. |

### Relationships and Justifications

- **G1 -> G2, G3 [;]**  
  - **Justification**: The mission requires sequential execution of collection followed by delivery.

- **G2 -> AT1.1, AT1.2 [OR]**  
  - **Justification**: Multiple storage locations can be handled independently, allowing any one to complete the task.

- **G3 -> AT2.1, AT2.2 [AND]**  
  - **Justification**: All deliveries must be completed for the mission to succeed.

### Summary

The goal model is structured to ensure resources are collected from multiple storage locations and then delivered to their respective destinations. Each phase (collection and delivery) is handled sequentially, with collection tasks being independent (OR decomposition) and delivery tasks requiring all to complete (AND decomposition). This ensures efficient resource management and mission success.
